// Intimora — extra TL constructors, layer 231
//
// The Telegram login (TELEGRAM_SESSION) was exported by a layer-231 client and
// Telegram keeps answering that auth key at layer 231, while MadelineProto
// 8.21.2 parses with the layer-233 scheme. A layer-231 `channel` therefore has
// an id the parser does not know, and TL deserialization throws:
//
//   danog\MadelineProto\TL\Exception: Could not extract type: Chat with id
//   d49f34c6, you should update MadelineProto!
//
// That error escapes from the read loop and kills the whole PHP request with a
// fatal error instead of JSON — which is what the video list, the premium
// ledger and the stream routes were doing.
//
// These are the layer-231 definitions of every constructor that changed in
// 232/233 (only these five; the rest of the schema is identical). They are
// loaded as a separate scheme through Settings\TLSchema::setOther() in
// mtproto.php and tagged ===231===, so the layer-233 definitions of the same
// predicates stay untouched and objects of either layer parse.

---types---

===231===
